Commit Messages for Bug Fixes

Example of a good bug-fix commit message:

Fix login error when users enter an invalid password

Characteristics of a well-written commit message:

1. Clear and specific
   It clearly explains what was changed.

2. Short and concise
   It describes the change directly without unnecessary information.

3. Uses an action word
   It begins with an action word such as Fix, Add, Update, Remove, or Improve.

4. Relevant to the change
   It accurately describes the changes made.

A good commit message helps team members understand the project's history.
